	"description": [
		"Students explore a specified topic or theme in language, in literature or in culture/civilization, or in a combination of these, through close reading, discussion, analysis and interpretation of selected literary and/or non-literary works. Sample topics include \"Madness and the Romantic Dream,\" \"Female Identity in Post-Colonial North Africa,\" and \"Global Francophone Identities.\" May be repeated if topics are different. Taught in French. Prerequisite: minimum of one 270-level course. Counts towards medieval studies major and Africa & the Americas concentration."
